8	82,282,150,970	Fig. 8.	The single pistil of the Morning-Glory, enlarged: a small ovary at the base, a long slender style, and a knobbed stigma at the top.
9	1402,868,1553,1525	Fig. 9.	A Lily stamen: a long curving filament, f, bearing an oblong anther, a, with grains of pollen scattered about it.
